From 9ccc96288dfa8ecb3e331e6df757f944943f7cbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:31:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add dual-head consistency distillation (DHCD) for the
 NMS-free head

YOLO26 supervises its NMS-free head with a single positive per object (tal_topk2=1)
while Progressive Loss decays the one-to-many weight to 0.1, so that head stays
under-confident and misses small objects that the one-to-many head detects. DHCD
matches the one-to-one posteriors to the one-to-many posteriors on the anchors the
teacher fires on (max class probability > 0.1), weighted by dhcd_w. The teacher is
read under no_grad, so only the student receives gradient, the one-to-many branch is
bit-identical to before, and inference cost is unchanged.
